    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/eu-gastwissenschaftlerin-wiss-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-im-bereich-theoretische-optik-photonik-dr-160-26": {
      "title": "EU Visiting Researcher / Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the field of Theoretical Optics & Photonics",
      "description": "EU Visiting Researcher / Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the field of Theoretical Optics & Photonics expected full-time employment - non-tariff compensation (third-party funding limited until 30.09.2029) At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Physics Location Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin Reference number DR/160/26 Time limitation 30. Sep 2029 Job scope Vollzeit Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 28. Oct 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific research services in the field of theoretical physics modelling light-matter interactions in nano-photonic systems collaboration with the research groups of the MSCA Doctoral Network QUEST What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed scientific university degree (Master’s or equivalent) in physics or a closely related field, preferably with an above-average grade in-depth knowledge of and a strong interest in theoretical physics proven mathematical skills and proficiency in at least one programming language (e.g., C++, Python, Julia) in-depth knowledge of the theory of light-matter interaction is desirable excellent communication and teamwork skills, along with active participation in network meetings, training schools, and outreach activities willingness to undertake research stays (secondments) of at least three months each at Sorbonne Paris Nord University (FR) and the European Laboratory for Non-Linear Spectroscopy (IT) maximum of 12 months of residence or main activity in Germany within the last 36 months prior to recruitment (MSCA mobility rule) fluency in English, both written and spoken (at least B2) What would be desirable in-depth knowledge of the theory of light-matter interaction What we offer a modern work environment high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding flexible working hours (flexitime) excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Non-tariff compensation, based on the flat rates specified in the EU Call 2025 (comprising a monthly living allowance, mobility allowance, and, if applicable, family allowance; each before deduction of statutory taxes and social security contributions). Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/160/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Physics, Theoretical Optics & Photonics Group, Prof. Dr. Kurt Busch (Location: Newtonstr. 15, 12489 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin, or preferably as a single PDF file via email to kurt.busch ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Kurt Busch ( kurt.busch ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on the earliest possible date. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Kurt Busch Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-82452 Email: kurt.busch ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Kurt Busch Department of Physics Address Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-82000 idir.physik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
