    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-auf-dem-gebiet-der-mikrosoziologie-an-196-26": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Field of Microsociology",
      "description": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Field of Microsociology 2/3-Teilzeitbeschäftigung max. befristet auf 6 Jahre gemäß WissZeitVG - E 13 TV-L HU At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences Department of Social Sciences Location Institutsgebäude, Universitätsstraße 3b, 10117 Berlin Reference number AN/196/26 Time limitation in months 72 Pay grade E13 Job scope Teilzeit (26.26 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 21. Oct 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific service in research and teaching in the field of sociology or demography teaching and coordination tasks within the framework of the BA and MA programs in Social Sciences (including support of exams) tasks for personal scientific qualification (doctorate) What you bring to the table completed scientific university education (preferably above-average degree) in Sociology or Demography research focus and teaching experience in at least one of the areas of Social Inequality, Life Course, Social Demography, Family, Cross-national Comparison, Quantitative and/or Qualitative Methods preferably publications in internationally recognized scientific journals and experience in the collection and/or analysis of social science data proficiency in spoken and written English (at least C1 level) good German language skills (at least A2 level) What we offer a modern work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding flexible working hours (flexitime) excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete, referencing the job ID AN/196/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Culture, Social Sciences and Education, Institute of Social Sciences, Prof. Dr. Anette Fasang (office location: Universitätsstr. 3b), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to gabi.sonnenberg ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ sowi.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: cover letter tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) performance evaluations contact details for two references If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Frau Gabi Sonnenberg gabi.sonnenberg ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ sowi.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . The position is scheduled to be filled on 01.03.2027. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. Anette Eva Fasang Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-66522 Email: anette.fasang ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ sowi.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr. Anette Eva Fasang Department of Social Sciences Address Institutsgebäude, Universitätsstraße 3b, 10117 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-66500 sowi.sekretariat ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/w3-professur-fuer-psychologische-methodenlehre-pr-009-26": {
      "title": "Full Professorship for ‘Psychological Research Methods’ (W3)",
      "description": "Full Professorship for ‘Psychological Research Methods’ (W3) to be appointed at the next possible date At a glance Job category Professorships and junior professorships Organization Faculty of Life Sciences Department of Psychology Location Rudower Chaussee 18, 12489 Berlin Adlershof Reference number PR/009/26 Pay grade W3 Job scope Vollzeit (40 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 03. Nov 2026 Apply now The Faculty of Life Sciences, Institute of Psychology, invites applications for a Full Professorship for ‘Psychological Research Methods’ (W3) to be appointed at the next possible date. Your responsibilities The future holder of this position should cover the entire spectrum of psychological methodology and teach courses in the bachelor's and master's degree programs in psychology. The position seeks a scientist with excellent scientific credentials and international visibility through publications and third-party funding, as well as international visibility. The professorship is anchored in the Human Developmental Dynamics focus area of the Institute of Psychology and at the same time forms the methodological basis for the entire discipline. It is desirable that the research profile fits this focus area and that the candidate has proven expertise in the field of multivariate statistics, especially in longitudinal data modeling. A willingness to collaborate with other disciplines is required. The W3 professorship includes a teaching load of 9 SWS. Teaching duties include the modules Methodology I and II in the bachelor's program as well as introductory and advanced modules in methodology in all master programs of the institute. The professorship is located on the Campus Berlin Adlershof. What you bring to the table The applicants must meet the legal requirements for professorial appointments in accordance with § 100 of the `Berliner Hochschulgesetz`. HU is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Researchers from abroad are welcome to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Your path to the HU Please send your application, referencing the job ID PR/009/26 preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to: berufungen.lewi ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de or to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Life Sciences, Dean, Prof. Dr. Dr. Christian Ulrichs, Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. Applications should include a (1) a cover letter, (2) a CV, (3) a teaching concept including a summary of teaching experience or evaluations (max. 3 pages), (4) a research concept describing the candidate's current research program and proposed research (max. 3 pages), (5) a list of publications up to five full copies of selected articles, (6) a statement (max. 1 page) identifying previous and future contributions to equity, diversity and inclusion, and the candidate’s ability to work in culturally diverse groups, (7) copies of certificates (including transcripts). Please also take note of the instructions concerning application documents on our web-site: https://hu.berlin/lewi_berufung . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Dr. rer. agr. Christian Ulrichs Dean Tel.: +49 30 2093-46312 Email: christian.ulrichs ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Dr. rer. agr. Christian Ulrichs Department of Psychology Address Wolfgang-Köhler-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 18, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-9340"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/w3-s-professur-fuer-literatur-und-kulturforschung-verbunden-mit-der-position-als-direktorin-m-w-d-des-leibniz-zentrums-fuer-literatur-und-kulturforschung-zfl-pr-004-26": {
      "title": "W3-S-Professor for “Literary and Cultural Research”  combined with the position of  Director (m/f/d) of the Leibniz Center for Literary and Cultural Research (ZfL)",
      "description": "W3-S-Professor for “Literary and Cultural Research” combined with the position of Director (m/f/d) of the Leibniz Center for Literary and Cultural Research (ZfL) At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences Department of Cultural History, Cultural Theory, and Media Studies Location Pergamonpalais, Georgenstraße 47, 10117 Berlin Reference number PR/004/26 Pay grade W3 Job scope Vollzeit Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 23. Oct 2026 Apply now The Leibniz Center for Literary and Cultural Research (ZfL) and Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin (HU), seek to appoint a W3-S-Professor for “Literary and Cultural Research” combined with the position of Director (m/f/d) of the Leibniz Center for Literary and Cultural Research (ZfL) by 01 April, 2028. The S-Professorship will be located at one of the institutes of the Faculty of Language, Literature and Humanities or at the Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences –Department of Cultural History, Cultural Theory, and Media Studies. The appointment will be made in a joint procedure by the Leibniz Center for Literary and Cultural Research and Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin with a reduced teaching load (equivalent to 2 LVS) at HU. The ZfL is a non-university research institute under the organizational umbrella of the Geisteswissenschaftliche Zentren Berlin e.V. (GWZ) and belongs to the Leibniz Association. It currently employs approximately 35 people in research and academic services. The position is to be filled by a person who will become the head of the ZfL as academic director (m/f/d), is familiar with the German and international academic system, and represents the center's research both within and outside the institution, particularly at the interface between academia, the public, and politics. The profile of the professorship covers the broad spectrum of literary research from a comparative and cultural research perspective ( https://www.zfl-berlin.org/institutsprofil.html ) . The personality being sought is an international leader in theoretical and methodological reflection within literary and/or cultural research and has exceptional innovative potential in developing and establishing new fields of research. At HU, they represent literary and cultural studies in research and teaching and cooperate with the colleagues of both faculties. Moreover, active participation in existing and future research networks in the Berlin/Brandenburg scientific community is expected. Clear ideas are also expected regarding the programmatic and structural development of the ZfL's research profile against the backdrop of the existing connection between basic research and socially relevant transfer formats. Leadership skills and experience in managing research institutions or research networks and in human resources management are required, as is experience in strategic planning, acquisition, and implementation of national and international research projects. The academic director, together with the other members of the executive board of Geisteswissenschaftliche Zentren Berlin e.V. (GWZ), is responsible for its overall management. The scope of duties is set out in the GWZ statutes in their currently valid version ( https://www.gwz-berlin.de/wp-content/uploads/gwz-satzung-210212.pdf ) . The S-Professorship comes with the obligation to teach courses equivalent to 2 LVS at one of the institutes of the Faculty of Language, Literature and Humanities or at the Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences – Department of Cultural History, Cultural Theory, and Media Studies; further involvement at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is desirable. The applicants must meet the legal requirements for professorial appointments in accordance with § 100 of the `Berliner Hochschulgesetz`. Your path to the HU HU is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Researchers from abroad are welcome to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Please send your application, referencing the job ID PR/004/26 to: Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Dean of the Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences, Prof. Becker, Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as one single PDF file to: berufungen.ksbf ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. Applications should include a (1) a cover letter, (2) a CV, (3) a teaching concept including a summary of teaching experience (max. 3 pages), (4) a research concept describing the candidate's current research program and proposed research in Literary and Cultural Research (max. 3 pages) as well as an outline of future research and development prospects for the ZfL for the next 5 to 10 years (approx. 5 pages), (5) a complete list of publications, (6) a statement (max. 1 page) identifying previous and future contributions to equity, diversity and inclusion, and the candidates ability to work in culturally diverse groups, (7) copies of certificates and diplomas, (8) contact details of up to three references, and (9) a description of the external funding secured. For questions regarding this position please contact berufungen.ksbf@hu-berlin.de. Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. Claudia Becker Dean Tel.: +49 30 2093-66152 Email: claudia.becker ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr. Claudia Becker Department of Cultural History, Cultural Theory, and Media Studies Address Pergamonpalais, Georgenstraße 47, 10117 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-66281"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-im-bereich-neuer-elektronischer-materialien-an-226-26": {
      "title": "Research fellow (m/f/d) in the field of novel electronic materials",
      "description": "Research fellow (m/f/d) in the field of novel electronic materials part-time employment (75 %) limited to 4 years - E 13 TV-L HU At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Physics Location Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin Reference number AN/226/26 Time limitation in months 48 Pay grade E13 Job scope Teilzeit (29.55 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 04. Nov 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific services in research and teaching in german language (3SWS fabrication and characterization of electronic materials, nano- and quantum structures setting up and conducting magneto-transport experiments in the Novel Materials group contributing to scientific exchange with national and international research cooperation partners tasks related to own scientific qualification (doctorate) What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed scientific university education in physics or materials science with a specialization in solid-state physics and above-average grades knowledge of semiconductor physics and technology proficiency in spoken and written German (at least C1) very good written and spoken English skills (at least B2) good knowledge of Microsoft Office, Origin, LabView, Python, e.g. ability to work independently and excellent experimental scientific skills ability to work in a team and cooperate with others What would be desirable fundamentals of knowledge transfer desired What we offer a modern work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding flexible working hours (flexitime) excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID AN/226/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Physik, Prof. Dr. Saskia F. Fischer (located: Newtonstr. 15, 12489 Berlin) or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to gnm ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations The position is scheduled to be filled on November 1, 2026. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Saskia F. Fischer Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-82202 Email: saskia.fischer ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr. rer. nat. Saskia F. Fischer Department of Physics Address Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-82000 idir.physik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
