    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-in-der-emmy-noether-forschungsgruppe-theoretical-transport-physics-t2p-dr-175-26": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P)",
      "description": "Research Fellow (m/f/d) in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P) expected 75 % part-time employment - E 13 TV-L HU (third-party funding limited for 9 month) At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Physics Location Zum Großen Windkanal 2, 12489 Berlin Reference number DR/175/26 Time limitation in months 9 Pay grade E13 Job scope Teilzeit (29.55 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 11. Nov 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities scientific service in research in the Emmy Noether research group Theoretical Transport Physics (T2P) timely attendance of regular meetings with the group carrying out analytical calculations implementing scientific software within the elphbolt code base carrying out numerical computations supporting collaborative work preparing manuscripts for publication presenting results at international conferences organizing internal events such as workshops and colloquiums What you bring to the table completed scientific university education (Master’s degree) in physics with a strong specialization in theoretical many-body physics evidenced by a Master’s thesis on the topic or a publication on the topic demonstrable experience in analytical calculations in the field of many-body physics demonstrable experience in developing parallel scientific software using modern Fortran within at least one open-source code base full professional proficiency (C1) in English Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID DR/175/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Physics, Dr. Nakib Protik (located: Zum Großen Windkanal 2, 12489 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de , entering <Your last name>_MT_2027_T2P in the subject line. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The application will be a single PDF file with just the following (and nothing else): Required application documents: letter of motivation (stating the motivation to join the T2P group, highlighting the fit to the stated requirements, and prior research experience) tabular curriculum vitae, including links to the Master’s thesis or published papers copies of certificates contact details of at least two reference letter writers (do not include the reference letters) Applications prepared in a different format will not be accepted. If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Dr. Nakib H. Protik ( nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ physik.hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on the earliest possible date. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Dr. Nakib Protik Nachwuchsgruppenleiter Tel.: +49 30 2093-82570 Email: nakib.protik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Dr. Nakib Protik Department of Physics Address Lise-Meitner-Haus, Newtonstraße 15, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-82000 idir.physik ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de"
    },
    "https://www.hu-berlin.de/en/university/working-at-the-hu/jobs/details/wissenschaftlicher-mitarbeiterin-m-w-d-im-bereich-technische-informatik-an-229-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Research Associate (m/f/d) in the field of Computer Engineering limited to 4 years - E 13 TV-L HU At a glance Job category Academic staff Organization Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Department of Computer Science Location Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin Reference number AN/229/26 Time limitation in months 48 Pay grade E13 Job scope Vollzeit (39.4 Hours weekly) Number of vacancies 1 Application deadline 11. Nov 2026 Apply now Founded in 1810, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is one of Germany's leading universities. As a comprehensive university with over 36,000 students, it combines research excellence with innovative support for young talents. Their international networks, interdisciplinary research collaborations, and progressive teaching concepts shape Berlin as a center of science. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin holds the status of a university of excellence. Your responsibilities research work in the field of Computer Engineering on the topic of reconfigurable processor architectures development, implementation and evaluation of novel hardware, including AI-assisted hardware, as well as the software for its programming and operation publication and presentation of research results at scientific conferences and in academic journals teaching duties amounting to 4 teaching hours per week (LVS) assisting with organisational tasks of the chair and with research grant applications tasks for personal scientific qualification (doctorate/PhD) What you bring to the table What we expect from you completed university degree (Master’s or equivalent) in engineering or a comparable field with a technical focus, or a computer science background excellent command of German, both written and spoken (at least C1-level) What would be desirable academic teaching experience in university courses What we offer a modern work environment a pay scale classification (TV-L) high responsibility in different working fields structured orientation and onboarding flexible working hours (flexitime) excellent opportunities for further training As a family-friendly university, we promote the compatibility of work and family life. Your path to the HU Please send your complete application, referencing the job ID AN/229/26 to Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Faculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science , Prof. Michael Hübner (located: Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin), Unter den Linden 6, 10099 Berlin or preferably in electronic form as a single PDF file to michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de . Required application documents: letter of motivation tabular curriculum vitae proof of the required qualification (certificates, diplomas, continuing education certificates) work references or evaluations If you have further questions about the job posting or the scope of duties, please do not hesitate to contact Prof. Michael Hübner ( michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de ). The position is scheduled to be filled on January 1, 2027. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is seeking to increase the proportion of women in research and teaching, and specifically encourages qualified female scholars to apply. Severely disabled applicants with equivalent qualifications will be given preferential consideration. People with an immigration history are specifically encouraged to apply. Since we will not return your documents, please submit copies in the application only. The Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin is bound by collective agreements and applies the TV-L HU. Information on pay grading and the annual salary scale can be found here: https://hu.berlin/ETRL . Information pursuant to Art. 12, 13 DSGVO on the processing of personal data at Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin within the framework of job advertisements can be found on our website: https://hu.berlin/DSGVO . Please visit our website which gives you access to the legally binding German version. Submit application Contact person Prof. Dr.-Ing. habil. Michael Hübner Professor Tel.: +49 30 2093-41252 Email: michael.huebner ☞ Please insert an @ at this point ☜ hu-berlin ☞ Please insert a period at this point de to profile page of Prof. Dr.-Ing. habil. Michael Hübner Department of Computer Science Address Johann-von-Neumann-Haus, Rudower Chaussee 25, 12489 Berlin General contact Tel.: +49 30 2093-41140"
    }
